License status of upstream
--------------------------
At the time of vendoring (April 2026) the trading-algo repository has no
LICENSE file in its root. Both reflexive-options and trading-algo are owned
by the same author (Mahimn Patel); this vendor is therefore an internal
author-to-author copy. The vendored files are re-licensed under the MIT
license that applies to the destination repository (see ./LICENSE).

Recommendation: add an explicit LICENSE file (MIT or Apache-2.0) to
trading-algo so that any future external use of these modules has an
unambiguous grant.

Modifications
-------------
The following modifications were made during vendoring:
- Patch import paths (`trading_algo.quant_core.models.atlas.*` →
  `reflexive_options.third_party.atlas.*`,
  `trading_algo.rat.*` → `reflexive_options.third_party.rat.*`).
- Strip trading-domain code (broker integration, options-wheel pricing,
  IBKR-specific helpers, hindsight-action scoring, execution_bridge,
  curriculum trainer, MLX backend, deprecated v7 variants).
- ``atlas/features.py``: inline minimal ``realized_volatility`` /
  ``iv_series_from_prices`` / ``iv_rank`` helpers from the upstream
  ``iv_rank`` module (which is itself trading-domain code and not vendored)
  and add an optional ``iv_series`` parameter to ``compute_features`` so
  callers can supply true implied-vol series from a simulator or quotes.
- ``atlas/inference.py``: drop the ``execution_bridge`` integration; the
  ``predict`` method now returns the raw (5,) action vector and callers
  map it to a domain decision via ``reflexive_options.rl.atlas_adapter``.
- ``rat/config.py``: inline the ``WeightingMethod`` enum (was imported
  from the unused ``rat.combiner`` subpackage).
- ``rat/attention/tracker.py``: remove the optional ``broker`` parameter
  to keep the module standalone.

The original ATLAS (Mamba state-space + cross-attention transformer, PPO/BC/EWC
training loops) and RAT (reflexivity meter, topology detector, attention flow
tracking) implementations remain attributable to the trading-algo project.

Domain-specific glue (state encoding, action interpretation, reward shaping,
options-env wiring) is implemented in this repository, not vendored:
see src/reflexive_options/rl/atlas_adapter.py and src/reflexive_options/rl/.
